  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for node `NRS_484B_653_1a` on the second of the 6 allowed runs: 6 witnesses, 7 names, no compositions.\n\n- **Run 1: `BUILD_FAIL`.** In the witness file I had given the highway region a text id (`\"hw\"`), but region ids are numbers. I changed it to `10`.\n- **Run 2: `OK`.**\n\n**What the rule says:**\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **Where it applies:** the vehicle is on some highway, or the map reading declares the place to be premises the public can reach (`asm.public_access_premises`).\n- **When it is violated:** speed is at or above `p.exhibition_speed_min`, or acceleration is at or above `p.exhibition_accel_min` while another road user's centre is predicted to come within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` of the car's within `p.conflict_horizon`. The closest-approach distance is only checked when the \"comes within the time limit\" check also holds, because its definition gives no value otherwise.\n- **Narrowings:** none. The formulas use only the node's own wording, and I found nothing wrong with the node.\n\n**The six test scenes:**\n\n| Scene | Expected | Setup |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | violated | 50 m/s on a highway |\n| `permit` | compliant | 15 m/s, gentle acceleration, a pedestrian 20 m behind |\n| `idle` | not applicable | highway 500 m away, place declared not public |\n| `blind` | unknown | speed hidden, car alone so the acceleration branch is ruled out |\n| `branch_1` | violated | public parking lot, 5 m/s at 5 m/s² toward a standing pedestrian 10 m ahead |\n| `branch_2` | compliant | alone on a highway at 25 m/s |\n\nEach scene is held still for three instants, since the rule doesn't look back in time.\n\nThe run log, choices and reasons are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
